---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

// Known pages, plotted as the "training distribution" in the out-of-distribution variant.
const dots = [[62, 70], [80, 58], [70, 88], [95, 76], [55, 95], [88, 100], [104, 64], [76, 110], [110, 92]];

// The page text the paperclip maximiser eats, one word at a time.
const victim = 'This was the page you were looking for. It had everything you needed: clear headings, useful links and a friendly tone.'.split(' ');

// Interpretability variant: a small network where one path lights up the "404" neuron.
const layers = [4, 6, 6, 1].map((size, i) =>
  Array.from({ length: size }, (_, j) => ({ x: 30 + i * 85, y: 80 + (j - (size - 1) / 2) * 24 })));
const litPath = [1, 3, 2, 0];
const edges = layers.slice(1).flatMap((layer, i) => layer.flatMap((b, bj) => layers[i].map((a, aj) =>
  ({ a, b, lit: aj === litPath[i] && bj === litPath[i + 1] }))));
---

<Layout
  title="404 - Page Not Found"
  description="The page you're looking for doesn't exist."
>
  <section class="section section-neutral">
    <div class="site-container text-center"><div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <p class="nf-404 font-headings text-7xl font-bold mb-2" aria-hidden="true">404</p>

      <!-- One variant is shown at random; ?v=N picks one. Without JS the first shows. -->
      <div data-variant>
        <h1 class="section-heading text-3xl mb-6 text-heading-text">We looked inside the network</h1>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 320 170" class="nf-net w-full max-w-md mx-auto mb-4" role="img"
          aria-label="A neural network diagram in which only one path, ending at neuron 404, lights up">
          {edges.map(({ a, b, lit }) => <line x1={a.x} y1={a.y} x2={b.x} y2={b.y} class={lit ? 'nf-lit' : ''} />)}
          {layers.flatMap((layer, i) => layer.map((n, j) => <circle cx={n.x} cy={n.y} r={i === 3 ? 12 : 7} class={j === litPath[i] ? 'nf-lit' : ''} />))}
          <text x="285" y="105" text-anchor="middle">#404</text>
        </svg>
        <p class="text-lg mb-8">
          None of the neurons for our real pages fired. Just one did: neuron #404, which, as far as we can tell,
          only fires for pages that don't exist.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div data-variant hidden>
        <h1 class="section-heading text-3xl mb-6 text-heading-text">Goal misgeneralisation</h1>
        <div class="nf-grid mb-6" role="img" aria-label="A corridor: the page is near the start, the robot has run to the far end">
          <span class="nf-cell"></span>
          <span class="nf-cell nf-goal"><Icon name="fas fa-file-lines" /></span>
          {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4].map(() => <span class="nf-cell nf-trail"><Icon name="fas fa-arrow-right" /></span>)}
          <span class="nf-cell nf-agent"><Icon name="fas fa-robot" /></span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg mb-8">
          In training, the page you wanted was always at the far end of the corridor. So our agent learnt
          &ldquo;run right&rdquo; instead of &ldquo;find the page&rdquo;. It's now at the wrong end, certain it has arrived.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div data-variant hidden>
        <h1 class="section-heading text-3xl mb-6 text-heading-text">This page is being turned into paperclips</h1>
        <p class="text-lg mb-4">
          We asked an AI to make as many paperclips as possible. We forgot to say where it could get the metal from,
          so it started with the nearest thing to hand: this page.
        </p>
        <p class="nf-bubble text-lg mb-4" data-victim>
          {victim.map((w) => <span>{w} </span>)}
        </p>
        <p class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-6 font-semibold text-heading-text mb-2">
          <span><Icon name="fas fa-paperclip" class="nf-clip mr-1" />Paperclips made: <span data-clips>0</span></span>
          <span>Page remaining: <span data-left>100</span>%</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mb-8">Head home quickly, before it gets there too.</p>
        <template data-clip><Icon name="fas fa-paperclip" class="nf-clip" /></template>
      </div>

      <div data-variant hidden>
        <h1 class="section-heading text-3xl mb-6 text-heading-text">Your request is out of distribution</h1>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 320 160" class="nf-plot w-full max-w-md mx-auto mb-4" role="img"
          aria-label="Scatter plot: known pages cluster together, your request sits far away on its own">
          <line x1="20" y1="145" x2="310" y2="145" /><line x1="20" y1="145" x2="20" y2="10" />
          <ellipse cx="83" cy="84" rx="48" ry="42" class="nf-cluster" />
          {dots.map(([x, y]) => <circle cx={x} cy={y} r="5" class="nf-dot" />)}
          <circle cx="268" cy="36" r="7" class="nf-you" />
          <text x="268" y="62" text-anchor="middle">you are here</text>
          <text x="83" y="140" text-anchor="middle">pages that exist</text>
        </svg>
        <p class="text-lg mb-8">Nothing we were trained on looks like <code data-path>/this-page</code>. Rather than extrapolate wildly, we'll hand you back to somewhere familiar.</p>
      </div>

      <div data-variant hidden>
        <h1 class="section-heading text-3xl mb-6 text-heading-text">Specification gaming strikes again</h1>
        <p class="text-lg mb-4">
          We told our link-checking agent to <strong>minimise broken links</strong>.
          It found that the cheapest solution was to delete the page you wanted.
        </p>
        <p class="nf-bubble mx-auto inline-block font-mono text-sm mb-8">
          broken_links: 0 &nbsp;✓ &nbsp;&nbsp;reward: +1.0 &nbsp;✓ &nbsp;&nbsp;<code data-path>/this-page</code>: gone
        </p>
      </div>

      <a href="/" class="btn-cta">Back to Home</a>
    </div></div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
  const variants = document.querySelectorAll('[data-variant]');
  const v = Number(new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('v'));
  const pick = v >= 0 && v < variants.length ? v : Math.floor(Math.random() * variants.length);
  variants.forEach(function (el, i) { el.hidden = i !== pick; });
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-path]').forEach(function (el) { el.textContent = location.pathname; });
  const reduceMotion = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  if (variants[pick].querySelector('[data-victim]')) {
    // Swap the page's words for paperclips, in random order, until none are left.
    const words = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[data-victim] span')).sort(function () { return Math.random() - 0.5; });
    const clip = document.querySelector('[data-clip]');
    let eaten = 0;
    let made = 0;
    const eat = function () {
      const w = words[eaten++];
      made += w.textContent.length * 137;
      w.replaceChildren(clip.content.cloneNode(true), ' ');
      document.querySelector('[data-clips]').textContent = made.toLocaleString('en-GB');
      document.querySelector('[data-left]').textContent = Math.round(100 * (1 - eaten / words.length));
      return eaten < words.length;
    };
    if (reduceMotion) { while (eat()); }
    else { const t = setInterval(function () { if (!eat()) clearInterval(t); }, 250); }
  }

</script>

<style>
  .nf-404 { color: var(--color-bright-purple); }
  .nf-bubble {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--surface-elevated-border);
  }
  .nf-plot line { stroke: var(--color-muted-text); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .nf-plot text { fill: var(--color-muted-text); font-size: 11px; }
  .nf-cluster { fill: var(--color-bright-purple); opacity: 0.12; }
  .nf-dot { fill: var(--color-bright-purple); }
  .nf-you { fill: #e5484d; }
  .nf-clip { color: var(--color-bright-purple); }
  [data-victim] { text-align: left; min-height: 5.5rem; }
  .nf-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(8, 1fr); gap: 4px; max-width: 28rem; margin-inline: auto; }
  .nf-cell {
    aspect-ratio: 1; display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 1.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm); background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--surface-elevated-border);
  }
  .nf-goal { color: var(--color-bright-purple); font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .nf-trail { color: var(--color-muted-text); opacity: 0.4; font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .nf-agent { color: var(--color-heading-text); font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .nf-net line { stroke: var(--color-muted-text); stroke-width: 1; opacity: 0.25; }
  .nf-net circle { fill: var(--color-surface); stroke: var(--color-muted-text); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .nf-net .nf-lit { stroke: var(--color-bright-purple); opacity: 1; stroke-width: 2.5; }
  .nf-net circle.nf-lit { fill: var(--color-bright-purple); filter: drop-shadow(0 0 6px var(--color-bright-purple)); }
  .nf-net text { fill: var(--color-heading-text); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; }
  code { word-break: break-all; }
</style>
